From: Aspartame GTK4 migration
Subject: [PATCH] controlpanel: release modal state when shell closes window

GTK4 Settings can be closed by a semantic shell action such as ShowHome or
ShowFrame.  Those paths call the window close operation directly; relying on
the old destroy callback leaves ShellModel.has_modal() true and blocks the
next Settings open.  Release the same ownership flag used by the stop button
before closing the panel.

--- a/src/jarabe/view/service.py
+++ b/src/jarabe/view/service.py
@@ -122,4 +122,7 @@ class UIService(service.Object):
         panel = getattr(self, '_control_panel', None)
         if panel is not None:
             panel.destroy()
             self._control_panel = None
+            if getattr(panel, '_has_modal', False):
+                panel._has_modal = False
+                self._shell_model.pop_modal()
